id=a52sxq_soundtrigger_no_hal_reboot
name=Sound trigger: HAL errors and callback mismatches no longer restart the audio HAL
author=kusti420
description=Hardening for the call audio report of 2026-10-22 ("I hear them for a second, then neither side hears anything", CS calls and WhatsApp, clean flash of the latest build). On the A52s vendor the sound trigger HAL lives inside the audio HAL process (android.hardware.audio.service), so every SoundTriggerHalEnforcer.reboot() kills the audio HAL: a running call loses its voice/VoIP session in both directions, and audioserver restarts. That is the only mechanism seen so far on this ROM that kills all call audio at once. It is proven in the 9.3.62 tester log (logsrecentes.txt: "Exception caught from HAL, rebooting HAL" -> media.audio_flinger died), and calls are exactly when the HAL is pushed onto its non-LPI path ("lpi NOT supported due to concurrency"), where the A52s ACDB has no LSM table for the Google model (-19). 9.3.63 (soundtrigger_load_no_reboot) only covered loadSoundModel/loadPhraseSoundModel. Any other HAL status error still rebooted the HAL: startRecognition, stopRecognition, unloadSoundModel, forceRecognitionEvent and the model parameter calls. So did the HAL callback contract checks: an event for an unknown model, recognitionStillActive with a non-success status, and an unload event for an unknown or active model. Changes: (1) SoundTriggerHalEnforcer.handleException turns a HalException (the HAL answered with a status code) into RecoverableException(5, INTERNAL_ERROR); the client sees an error, the HAL keeps running. (2) ModelCallbackEnforcer keeps its wtfStack log and drops the offending event instead of rebooting. Still rebooted: dead HALs (unchanged RecoverableException DEAD_OBJECT path), other runtime exceptions in handleException, and SoundTriggerHalWatchdog timeouts (a hung HAL). NOT proven to be the cause of the 2026-10-22 report. CallSim tests on R5CTA0ESFTF (no SIM) found no ST reboot and no audio loss. Those tests went through AudioService: IN_CALL plus Telecom g_call_state=2, IN_COMMUNICATION plus g_call_state=0x1200010 with VOICE_COMMUNICATION record and playback, and a VOICE_COMMUNICATION connect tone during IN_CALL. The tester logcat decides; grep it for SoundTriggerHalEnforcer / "not rebooting the HAL".
